  "id": "two-thousand-and-late",
  "title": "TWO THOUSAND AND LATE",
  "subtitle": "",
  "description": "GET READY TO WREAK SOME HAVOC! This new fiction podcast from the writer that brought you The Bright Sessions and Bridgewater follows the story of Harper, a thirty-six year old nihilist whose life is upended when she’s possessed by a demon hell-bent on bringing about the apocalypse. Harper doesn’t want to end the world, but the demon gives her more power than she’s had in her life in a long time. In a world where so many people abuse their power, will Harper be any different? TWO THOUSAND AND LATE blends sharp satire with genre flair and wickedly lovable antiheroes. It’s a potent cocktail of feminist rage, queer power, and supernatural mischief. An Atypical Artists production produced by Patrick Ellis and Lauren Shippen. For more information, go to harperandhavoc.com. To support the show, visit atypicalartists.co/support",
